# This vault syncs between macOS and Windows. Normalize every text file to LF —
# in the repo and on checkout — so line endings cannot ping-pong per machine.
# core.autocrlf is false, so without this git stores whatever endings whichever
# tool last wrote the file happened to use, and a one-line edit lands as a
# whole-file diff that hides what actually changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF on every OS so they run under bash (macOS/Linux
# and Git Bash on Windows). Overrides core.autocrlf, which would otherwise
# convert them to CRLF on Windows checkout and break the shebang/parsing.
# Covered by the rule above, but pinned explicitly so it survives any future
# loosening of it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries — never normalize.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary

# Template development plans are NOT part of the distributable template. They
# describe stripping the source vault and name its owner throughout, so they
# must never reach the exported repo. `export-ignore` makes `git archive` skip
# them automatically, rather than relying on remembering to delete them first.
#
# RULE: any plan written to build the template itself gets a line here.
.agents/plans/0-active/2026-08-28-onboard-command.md export-ignore
